  "unit": "u09-past",
  "title": "I didn't",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "To say 'didn't' or 'haven't', take the **present** form and add **-নি** (*-ni*), joined to the verb. One form covers both English meanings:\n\n- করি → **করিনি** 'I didn't do / haven't done'\n- খাই → **খাইনি** 'I didn't eat / haven't eaten'\n- খাও → **খাওনি** 'you didn't eat'\n- যাই → **যাইনি** 'I didn't go'\n- দেখি → **দেখিনি** 'I didn't see'\n- আসে → **আসেনি** 'he hasn't come'\n\nKeep apart: **খাই না** (two words) 'I don't eat' vs **খাইনি** (one word) 'I didn't eat'.\n\n**What about করলাম না?** Simple past + **না** usually means you *chose* not to: **আমি গেলাম না** 'I didn't go (I decided not to)'. For a plain 'didn't', use **-নি**.\n\n**এখনো** 'yet / still' goes well with -নি: **আমি এখনো খাইনি** 'I haven't eaten yet'. Short answer: **এখনো না** 'not yet'. **ইতিমধ্যে** 'already' goes with the perfect: **আমি ইতিমধ্যে খেয়েছি** (a bit formal).",
